An iPhone app in Swift and UIKit, built in code with a coordinator for navigation and MVVM screens.

## Requirements

- macOS with Xcode and an iOS simulator runtime <!-- stacks:fill: the Xcode, Swift and iOS deployment target versions recorded at setup -->
- XcodeGen and SwiftLint (`brew install xcodegen swiftlint`); xcbeautify is optional (`brew install xcbeautify`)
- swift-format comes with Xcode (`xcrun swift-format`)

## Getting started

```sh
make install   # check the toolchain and generate the Xcode project
make build     # build the app and test bundles for the simulator
make test      # unit tests
make test-ui   # UI smoke tests
open {{project_slug}}.xcodeproj
```

The `.xcodeproj` is generated from `project.yml` and not committed. Change targets and settings in `project.yml`, then run `make project`.

## Commands

| Command | What it does |
| --- | --- |
| `make install` | Check the toolchain and generate the Xcode project |
| `make project` | Regenerate the Xcode project from `project.yml` |
| `make build` | Build the app and both test bundles for a simulator; warnings fail |
| `make lint` | SwiftLint with warnings as errors |
| `make fmt` | Format Swift sources with swift-format |
| `make fmt-check` | Fail on any swift-format difference or finding |
| `make test` | Unit tests |
| `make coverage` | Unit tests with line coverage; fails below `COVERAGE_MIN` in the Makefile |
| `make test-ui` | UI smoke tests and accessibility audits on a simulator |
| `make ci` | Everything CI runs |
| `make clean` | Remove build output and the generated project |

Set `SIM_UDID` (or a full `SIM_DESTINATION`) to choose the simulator; otherwise the targets pick an available iPhone.

